invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: table_select returns without writing zero through the pointer
  its masks went through, so the word behind it ends on the last entry's
  mask: all ones when the digit was the last index and zero when it was
  not, one bit of the private exponent a step, in the dead frame.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test cannot look for it, because memory holds a word
  of all ones or of zeros for other reasons. inv-16-rsa-table-read
  refuses a table_select that does not end with that write.

--- old
    // volatile pointer, so no compiler may drop it.
    *hidden = 0;
--- new
    // volatile pointer, so no compiler may drop it.
